1
00:00:45,679 --> 00:00:46,600
What are you doing?

2
00:00:47,280 --> 00:00:47,679
Let go!

3
00:00:48,079 --> 00:00:48,880
Let go of me!

4
00:00:49,759 --> 00:00:50,799
What the hell do you want?

5
00:00:51,280 --> 00:00:52,119
Let me go!

6
00:00:52,840 --> 00:00:53,240
Let—

7
00:00:53,759 --> 00:00:54,240
Get in!

8
00:00:55,759 --> 00:00:56,399
What are you doing?

9
00:00:57,359 --> 00:00:58,079
Didn't I tell you...

10
00:00:58,119 --> 00:01:00,439
tell you to wait for me right there?

11
00:01:00,560 --> 00:01:01,719
You run pretty fast, huh?

12
00:01:01,799 --> 00:01:02,479
Still trying to run?

13
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:04,079
What do you want?

14
00:01:04,359 --> 00:01:05,120
What do I want?

15
00:01:05,120 --> 00:01:05,719
Where's the money?

16
00:01:06,760 --> 00:01:07,799
That money's mine now.

17
00:01:08,120 --> 00:01:09,319
I earned it drink by drink!

18
00:01:10,359 --> 00:01:11,000
Oh, please!

19
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:12,120
You really think you're worth that much?

20
00:01:12,120 --> 00:01:12,840
Ten thousand a glass?

21
00:01:13,120 --> 00:01:13,719
Where's your bag?

22
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Where's the bag? Don't touch me!

23
00:01:15,120 --> 00:01:15,719
Where's the bag?

24
00:01:16,480 --> 00:01:17,480
Where'd you hide the money?

25
00:01:18,480 --> 00:01:19,439
The money is mine!

26
00:01:19,640 --> 00:01:20,519
None of your business where I hid it!

27
00:01:22,280 --> 00:01:23,280
So you want to...

28
00:01:23,439 --> 00:01:24,359
save it for your son, huh?

29
00:01:25,599 --> 00:01:26,040
Leizi!

30
00:01:26,200 --> 00:01:27,000
Drive to her place.

31
00:01:27,519 --> 00:01:28,400
Don't you touch my son!

32
00:01:28,760 --> 00:01:29,920
Fine, I won't touch your son.

33
00:01:30,079 --> 00:01:31,560
Then I'll touch you instead.

34
00:01:31,640 --> 00:01:32,959
Don't... don't mess around!

35
00:01:33,599 --> 00:01:34,439
Let go!

36
00:01:34,599 --> 00:01:35,519
Let go of me!

37
00:01:36,640 --> 00:01:37,359
I'm telling you!

38
00:01:37,519 --> 00:01:38,680
Keep this up and I'll jump!

39
00:01:38,920 --> 00:01:39,719
Jump then! Go ahead!

40
00:01:39,879 --> 00:01:40,359
Jump!

41
00:01:40,439 --> 00:01:40,920
Leizi!

42
00:01:40,920 --> 00:01:41,640
Speed it up for her!

43
00:01:41,719 --> 00:01:42,159
Got it!

44
00:01:42,519 --> 00:01:43,640
Think I can't handle you?

45
00:01:44,280 --> 00:01:45,959
Swan meat doesn't even taste good.

46
00:01:48,920 --> 00:01:50,000
Pull over! Stop the car!

47
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:51,000
Pull over for what?

48
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:51,400
Boss...

49
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:52,359
It's pitch black outside.

50
00:01:52,519 --> 00:01:52,879
Leizi, what...

51
00:01:52,879 --> 00:01:53,840
what did you just say?

52
00:01:54,439 --> 00:01:55,480
Who're you calling a swan?

53
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:57,159
If she's a swan, what am I?

54
00:01:57,280 --> 00:01:57,640
I... uh...

55
00:01:57,760 --> 00:01:58,359
Stop the car!

56
00:01:58,519 --> 00:01:59,000
Hurry up!

57
00:02:02,640 --> 00:02:03,879
Oh, for God's sake!

58
00:02:04,760 --> 00:02:06,280
Piss off, both of you! Get out!

59
00:02:06,879 --> 00:02:08,159
Boss, it's freezing out there!

60
00:02:08,319 --> 00:02:09,319
It's over thirty below zero!

61
00:02:09,680 --> 00:02:10,199
Get out!

62
00:02:10,479 --> 00:02:11,039
Come on, Boss...

63
00:02:11,039 --> 00:02:11,599
You... you...

64
00:02:11,759 --> 00:02:13,120
just do whatever you want!

65
00:02:13,120 --> 00:02:13,919
We won't look!

66
00:02:14,080 --> 00:02:14,960
I'll close my eyes, completely shut!

67
00:02:15,479 --> 00:02:16,520
Get out of the car, hear me?

68
00:02:19,159 --> 00:02:19,960
Come on, let's go see.

69
00:02:21,639 --> 00:02:22,319
Chase her!

70
00:02:24,639 --> 00:02:25,199
How did she...

71
00:02:25,560 --> 00:02:26,560
How'd she wake up?

72
00:02:30,560 --> 00:02:31,120
Don't run!

73
00:02:31,479 --> 00:02:32,439
Don't let her get away!

74
00:02:33,479 --> 00:02:33,919
Right!

75
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:47,039
Are you okay?

76
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:50,680
Are you all right?

77
00:02:52,919 --> 00:02:53,639
What's going on?

78
00:02:53,639 --> 00:02:54,080
What's wrong with her?

79
00:02:54,120 --> 00:02:55,240
Why is she convulsing?

80
00:02:55,280 --> 00:02:55,719
Boss!

81
00:02:55,840 --> 00:02:56,199
Boss!

82
00:02:56,599 --> 00:02:57,199
What do we do?

83
00:02:57,479 --> 00:02:57,840
What now?

84
00:02:57,840 --> 00:02:58,840
Stop bullshitting!

85
00:02:59,400 --> 00:03:00,199
What do we do, Boss?

86
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:01,080
This...

87
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:02,840
Should we take her to the hospital?

88
00:03:03,400 --> 00:03:03,960
We can't take her to the hospital.

89
00:03:03,960 --> 00:03:04,840
If we take her to the hospital,

90
00:03:04,960 --> 00:03:06,280
won't they know we did it?

91
00:03:06,759 --> 00:03:07,479
What do we do then?

92
00:03:07,599 --> 00:03:08,520
We just won the bid on the factory.

93
00:03:08,520 --> 00:03:09,439
Nothing can happen to the factory.

94
00:03:09,439 --> 00:03:09,960
Then what do we do?

95
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:12,439
How about we take her home?

96
00:03:12,639 --> 00:03:13,599
Do you even know where she lives?

97
00:03:13,639 --> 00:03:14,319
"Take her home"?

98
00:03:14,599 --> 00:03:15,439
Then what else can we do?

99
00:03:15,520 --> 00:03:16,400
What do we do, Boss?

100
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:19,879
Say something!

101
00:03:19,879 --> 00:03:20,400
What do we do?

102
00:03:20,439 --> 00:03:21,520
You make the call!

103
00:03:21,919 --> 00:03:23,159
Take her back where she came from.

104
00:03:23,319 --> 00:03:23,719
Right, right, right.

105
00:03:23,719 --> 00:03:24,159
Okay, okay, okay.

106
00:03:25,479 --> 00:03:26,039
Get her...

107
00:03:26,280 --> 00:03:27,080
Lift, lift, lift!

108
00:03:27,120 --> 00:03:27,719
Okay, into the car!

109
00:03:51,520 --> 00:03:52,120
Listen to me.

110
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:53,520
In a bit,

111
00:03:53,879 --> 00:03:55,120
we put her back exactly the same.

112
00:03:55,120 --> 00:03:55,719
Got it?

113
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:57,400
Just like she was before.

114
00:03:57,400 --> 00:03:59,120
Put her clothes on nice and neat.

115
00:03:59,120 --> 00:03:59,639
Understand?

116
00:03:59,680 --> 00:04:00,159
Got it.

117
00:04:00,319 --> 00:04:03,400
Whoever asks, we don't know a thing.

118
00:04:03,599 --> 00:04:04,719
We never saw her.

119
00:04:04,719 --> 00:04:05,319
You hear me?

120
00:04:05,599 --> 00:04:06,280
Drive faster.

121
00:04:06,400 --> 00:04:07,159
Go, go, go.

122
00:06:58,439 --> 00:06:59,439
Both master and apprentice confessed.

123
00:07:01,079 --> 00:07:02,519
Your voice is completely hoarse.

124
00:07:02,720 --> 00:07:03,360
Have some water first.

125
00:07:05,319 --> 00:07:06,480
Liu Tieping confessed.

126
00:07:06,560 --> 00:07:08,360
He said he committed all the crimes.

127
00:07:08,519 --> 00:07:10,560
And in that basement of the old brewery,

128
00:07:10,639 --> 00:07:12,480
they found Feiyun-brand snow boots.

129
00:07:12,480 --> 00:07:13,360
Size 45.

130
00:07:13,720 --> 00:07:15,680
And the shoeprint at Qian Yichuan's crime scene,

131
00:07:15,720 --> 00:07:16,519
it's an exact match.

132
00:07:16,519 --> 00:07:18,279
So the chain of evidence is complete.

133
00:07:18,480 --> 00:07:19,480
But as for Cheng Youtian,

134
00:07:19,519 --> 00:07:21,519
I think he wants to protect his apprentice,

135
00:07:21,879 --> 00:07:23,480
so he insists he did everything himself.

136
00:07:25,399 --> 00:07:26,600
What about the beer bottle caps?

137
00:07:28,959 --> 00:07:29,560
He said he tossed them.

138
00:07:30,240 --> 00:07:31,079
Tossed them where?

139
00:07:31,439 --> 00:07:32,199
He said he forgot.

140
00:07:33,040 --> 00:07:34,040
Forgot?

141
00:07:36,199 --> 00:07:39,279
Shen Leshui, Liu Tieping, and Liu Xiaosheng...

142
00:07:39,319 --> 00:07:40,680
all three of them, without exception,

143
00:07:40,720 --> 00:07:41,560
mentioned a sum of money.

144
00:07:42,399 --> 00:07:44,040
Liu Tieping said

145
00:07:44,399 --> 00:07:45,800
he learned from Ma Guowen that

146
00:07:46,160 --> 00:07:48,120
on December 31, 1999,

147
00:07:48,480 --> 00:07:50,439
Ma Guowen gave Liu Xuemei some money.

148
00:07:50,600 --> 00:07:51,560
200,000 in cash.

149
00:07:51,759 --> 00:07:54,120
Yet the money's whereabouts are still unknown.

150
00:07:54,399 --> 00:07:56,199
Liu Tieping said his biggest regret

151
00:07:56,439 --> 00:07:57,319
was acting on impulse

152
00:07:57,319 --> 00:07:58,759
and killing Ma Guowen right then and there,

153
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:00,199
without getting a confession out of him.

154
00:08:00,920 --> 00:08:02,160
Liu Xiaosheng claimed

155
00:08:02,160 --> 00:08:03,360
he never saw that money.

156
00:08:06,759 --> 00:08:07,720
Earlier,

157
00:08:08,079 --> 00:08:08,920
Shen Leshui mentioned

158
00:08:08,920 --> 00:08:10,279
back on the day of the auction,

159
00:08:10,279 --> 00:08:11,800
she did see Liu Xuemei

160
00:08:11,800 --> 00:08:13,839
carrying a bulging plaid cloth bag.

161
00:08:13,959 --> 00:08:15,600
Yet at the scene of the death,

162
00:08:15,600 --> 00:08:16,399
that bag was nowhere to be found.

163
00:08:16,839 --> 00:08:18,279
I checked the case files from back then,

164
00:08:18,279 --> 00:08:19,800
and the bag definitely wasn't at the scene.

165
00:08:21,079 --> 00:08:22,319
Liu Xiaosheng said

166
00:08:22,560 --> 00:08:24,839
the last time he saw Liu Xuemei,

167
00:08:25,160 --> 00:08:26,279
he didn't see the bag either.

168
00:08:26,399 --> 00:08:27,519
Liu Tieping suspected

169
00:08:27,600 --> 00:08:29,720
that Shen Leshui took the 200,000 yuan.

170
00:08:29,839 --> 00:08:31,519
Shen Leshui insists she didn't take it.

171
00:08:33,200 --> 00:08:34,399
So the 200,000 just vanished into thin air?

172
00:08:34,399 --> 00:08:35,000
Right?

173
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:37,840
Right now,

174
00:08:38,240 --> 00:08:40,159
just as we're getting somewhere on the serial killings,

175
00:08:40,559 --> 00:08:41,759
a theft case pops up out of nowhere.

176
00:08:42,600 --> 00:08:43,960
Your old classmate said

177
00:08:44,480 --> 00:08:46,399
she has to track down that money,

178
00:08:46,519 --> 00:08:48,080
or she won't leave Lacheng.

179
00:08:52,200 --> 00:08:53,799
Tell her to stay out of trouble.

180
00:08:54,919 --> 00:08:56,039
Don't make a mess of things.

181
00:08:57,320 --> 00:08:58,559
We'll look into this.

182
00:09:03,360 --> 00:09:04,840
Even a poor home holds a fortune.

183
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:05,559
I mean,

184
00:09:06,240 --> 00:09:07,200
the moment you talk about moving,

185
00:09:07,879 --> 00:09:10,159
all the bags and bundles come pouring out.

186
00:09:16,759 --> 00:09:18,080
Why are you just standing there?

187
00:09:18,080 --> 00:09:19,120
Come help me.

188
00:09:20,639 --> 00:09:21,200
Mom.

189
00:09:23,240 --> 00:09:24,279
Did you...

190
00:09:24,960 --> 00:09:25,879
lose a bag?

191
00:09:29,200 --> 00:09:31,120
I'd used that bag for over ten years.

192
00:09:31,159 --> 00:09:31,679
It's fine.

193
00:09:32,320 --> 00:09:33,440
You know that thief?

194
00:09:33,679 --> 00:09:34,759
It's so bizarre.

195
00:09:35,320 --> 00:09:36,120
They took the bag,

196
00:09:36,120 --> 00:09:37,120
but my wallet...

197
00:09:37,240 --> 00:09:37,919
left it right there.

198
00:09:41,240 --> 00:09:42,039
That bag...

199
00:09:42,480 --> 00:09:43,600
how did you get it?

200
00:09:43,919 --> 00:09:44,840
Found it.

201
00:09:45,279 --> 00:09:46,240
Where did you find it?

202
00:09:47,519 --> 00:09:48,440
In the trash can.

203
00:09:48,879 --> 00:09:49,799
Which trash can?

204
00:09:49,919 --> 00:09:50,480
Downstairs.

205
00:09:52,279 --> 00:09:53,200
When was this?

206
00:09:53,960 --> 00:09:56,360
That snowy day back then.

207
00:09:57,919 --> 00:09:58,960
The millennium...

208
00:09:59,559 --> 00:10:00,639
Winter of 2000.

209
00:10:02,440 --> 00:10:03,360
Who threw it away?

210
00:10:03,960 --> 00:10:04,720
Haipeng.

211
00:10:07,080 --> 00:10:08,120
Zhao Haipeng?

212
00:10:10,399 --> 00:10:11,240
Yeah, Haipeng.

213
00:10:11,720 --> 00:10:12,840
That spendthrift.

214
00:10:14,480 --> 00:10:15,679
When you picked up that bag,

215
00:10:15,679 --> 00:10:16,799
was it empty?

216
00:10:18,120 --> 00:10:19,879
Would he dare throw it out if there was stuff in it?

217
00:10:23,120 --> 00:10:23,759
Mom.

218
00:10:24,559 --> 00:10:24,960
Mom.

219
00:10:25,120 --> 00:10:26,000
Could you, could you...

220
00:10:26,039 --> 00:10:26,879
tell me about it?

221
00:10:26,879 --> 00:10:27,679
What really happened?

222
00:10:27,799 --> 00:10:29,399
Like, Zhao Haipeng...

223
00:10:29,480 --> 00:10:31,320
How did he bring the bag over?

224
00:10:31,759 --> 00:10:32,679
When he showed up,

225
00:10:32,679 --> 00:10:33,919
was there anything inside it?

226
00:10:34,320 --> 00:10:35,279
Think carefully.

227
00:10:36,080 --> 00:10:38,000
It's been so many years.

228
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:39,240
Why are you suddenly asking about it,

229
00:10:39,240 --> 00:10:40,600
going on and on?

230
00:10:40,600 --> 00:10:41,960
Just help me think back.

231
00:10:42,480 --> 00:10:43,720
What really happened that day?

232
00:10:43,840 --> 00:10:45,200
How did he bring the bag over?

233
00:10:47,879 --> 00:10:49,840
Well, he came the night before,

234
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:52,159
came again in the morning,

235
00:10:52,639 --> 00:10:53,279
and came again at noon.

236
00:10:53,279 --> 00:10:54,080
So I asked him.

237
00:10:54,399 --> 00:10:55,840
I said, "Why are you here again?"

238
00:10:57,639 --> 00:10:58,639
When I saw him come,

239
00:10:58,840 --> 00:11:00,000
I went out to buy some bean paste.

240
00:11:00,360 --> 00:11:01,519
Wanted to make him some...

241
00:11:01,960 --> 00:11:02,759
meat sauce.

242
00:11:02,799 --> 00:11:04,519
Mom, get to the point.

243
00:11:04,759 --> 00:11:06,120
Wasn't I out buying paste?

244
00:11:06,200 --> 00:11:07,039
And then?

245
00:11:07,279 --> 00:11:08,559
Then I bought minced meat,

246
00:11:09,480 --> 00:11:09,960
and the paste.

247
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:11,399
Get to the point. Aren't you—

248
00:11:12,240 --> 00:11:12,600
No...

249
00:11:12,600 --> 00:11:14,480
What is the point?

250
00:11:14,759 --> 00:11:15,960
Zhao Haipeng.

251
00:11:16,320 --> 00:11:17,080
When he arrived,

252
00:11:17,080 --> 00:11:18,440
was he carrying that bag?

253
00:11:19,440 --> 00:11:20,759
When he arrived...

254
00:11:21,720 --> 00:11:22,480
Oh, right.

255
00:11:22,840 --> 00:11:24,519
Wasn't he wearing that overcoat?

256
00:11:24,519 --> 00:11:25,120
Just like this,

257
00:11:25,759 --> 00:11:26,399
bundled up,

258
00:11:26,759 --> 00:11:27,799
all hunched over.

259
00:11:29,559 --> 00:11:31,759
But I didn't see anything on him.

260
00:11:34,360 --> 00:11:35,440
Then why did you say

261
00:11:35,639 --> 00:11:37,559
he threw the bag in the trash?

262
00:11:37,919 --> 00:11:39,600
Wasn't I walking back from buying paste?

263
00:11:39,799 --> 00:11:41,120
I'd also bought minced meat.

264
00:11:41,519 --> 00:11:43,639
When I got back, I saw Zhao Haipeng

265
00:11:43,840 --> 00:11:44,759
take that bag,

266
00:11:44,759 --> 00:11:45,519
and toward the trash can,

267
00:11:45,639 --> 00:11:46,399
bam, tossed it right in!

268
00:11:46,399 --> 00:11:47,679
Then he rode off on his bicycle.

269
00:11:48,440 --> 00:11:49,320
So I figured

270
00:11:49,399 --> 00:11:50,480
he was throwing out my stuff,

271
00:11:50,480 --> 00:11:50,960
right?

272
00:11:51,320 --> 00:11:52,519
So I ran over to the trash can,

273
00:11:52,519 --> 00:11:53,399
fished it out, and saw

274
00:11:54,519 --> 00:11:55,960
the bag was still pretty new.

275
00:11:56,159 --> 00:11:56,759
Then I thought

276
00:11:56,759 --> 00:11:58,360
you must've disliked it,

277
00:11:58,360 --> 00:11:58,960
right?

278
00:11:59,200 --> 00:12:00,480
So I used it for groceries.

279
00:12:00,600 --> 00:12:01,320
Worked great.

280
00:12:10,039 --> 00:12:11,039
Are you okay?

281
00:12:15,480 --> 00:12:16,440
N-No, I'm fine.

282
00:12:20,200 --> 00:12:20,879
Mom.

283
00:12:22,360 --> 00:12:24,080
Haipeng and I...

284
00:12:24,960 --> 00:12:26,159
all these years since we split,

285
00:12:27,120 --> 00:12:29,320
has he been visiting you often?

286
00:12:29,559 --> 00:12:30,080
Yeah.

287
00:12:30,759 --> 00:12:32,559
Right up until he remarried,

288
00:12:33,080 --> 00:12:34,399
he was always dropping by.

289
00:12:34,480 --> 00:12:35,279
I figured

290
00:12:35,399 --> 00:12:37,080
he definitely wanted to get back with you.

291
00:12:37,080 --> 00:12:37,840
Right?

292
00:12:38,759 --> 00:12:39,480
And remember that year

293
00:12:39,480 --> 00:12:41,039
when my heart condition flared up?

294
00:12:41,440 --> 00:12:42,799
If it hadn't been for Haipeng,

295
00:12:42,919 --> 00:12:43,480
honestly,

296
00:12:43,480 --> 00:12:44,919
I wouldn't be alive today.

297
00:12:45,440 --> 00:12:46,879
Right, I told you about that.

298
00:12:49,279 --> 00:12:50,440
I've always believed

299
00:12:52,159 --> 00:12:53,320
he's a good man.

300
00:12:53,480 --> 00:12:54,120
He is.

301
00:12:54,840 --> 00:12:56,799
Haipeng really is a good boy.

302
00:12:58,399 --> 00:13:00,480
No matter what happened, big or small,

303
00:13:01,120 --> 00:13:03,080
he was always there helping out.

304
00:13:03,679 --> 00:13:04,399
Right?

305
00:13:04,759 --> 00:13:05,919
More attentive than you ever were.

306
00:13:06,200 --> 00:13:08,279
Whether proposing or divorcing...

307
00:13:11,240 --> 00:13:11,799
Hold still.

308
00:13:11,840 --> 00:13:12,399
I know, I know.

309
00:13:12,440 --> 00:13:13,159
Wait, that hurts!

310
00:13:13,200 --> 00:13:14,480
Ow, ow, ow!

311
00:13:17,200 --> 00:13:19,320
Why are there still glass shards in your hair?

312
00:13:22,200 --> 00:13:23,320
Does it need stitches?

313
00:13:23,960 --> 00:13:25,399
You don't really have to get stitches.

314
00:13:29,240 --> 00:13:30,159
Maybe just a couple of stitches?

315
00:13:30,399 --> 00:13:31,399
Stitches are fine,

316
00:13:31,559 --> 00:13:33,639
but we'll have to shave all the hair around here.

317
00:13:34,279 --> 00:13:34,919
No stitches, then.

318
00:13:41,600 --> 00:13:42,679
Don't move now.

319
00:13:42,919 --> 00:13:43,559
Bear with it.

320
00:13:45,480 --> 00:13:46,120
How are you doing?

321
00:13:46,960 --> 00:13:47,799
Does it hurt a lot?

322
00:13:48,080 --> 00:13:48,799
I'm fine. It doesn't hurt.

323
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:53,000
It's all my fault today.

324
00:13:53,480 --> 00:13:54,440
I dragged you into this.

325
00:13:54,840 --> 00:13:56,879
Come on, what does it have to do with you?

326
00:13:58,039 --> 00:13:58,879
Besides, I...

327
00:14:00,759 --> 00:14:01,279
well...

328
00:14:01,919 --> 00:14:03,360
As someone in Security...

329
00:14:03,360 --> 00:14:03,840
wait, no,

330
00:14:04,519 --> 00:14:05,519
as someone in Publicity,

331
00:14:05,519 --> 00:14:06,879
protecting the equipment—

332
00:14:06,879 --> 00:14:08,120
isn't that just my duty?

333
00:14:11,440 --> 00:14:13,279
You saved my video camera.

334
00:14:13,759 --> 00:14:15,840
How can I ever thank you?

335
00:14:17,519 --> 00:14:18,799
Let me buy you hot pot.

336
00:14:19,279 --> 00:14:20,600
I should be the one treating you.

337
00:14:21,279 --> 00:14:21,879
Right.

338
00:14:22,559 --> 00:14:23,480
Fair enough.

339
00:14:24,240 --> 00:14:24,720
Sounds like a plan.

340
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:26,639
Mom.

341
00:14:26,960 --> 00:14:28,480
Could you help me out a little more?

342
00:14:29,120 --> 00:14:30,639
I need to buy some more tapes.

343
00:14:31,159 --> 00:14:32,879
Didn't you just buy some a few days ago?

344
00:14:33,879 --> 00:14:35,240
I've already used them up.

345
00:14:37,720 --> 00:14:39,639
Go ask the TV station for support, then.

346
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:44,039
Xiao Miao already snuck me three tapes.

347
00:14:44,440 --> 00:14:46,080
Any more and she won't be able to explain it.

348
00:14:46,120 --> 00:14:46,519
Come on,

349
00:14:46,519 --> 00:14:48,240
where am I supposed to get that kind of money?

350
00:14:50,919 --> 00:14:51,919
Mom, look,

351
00:14:52,120 --> 00:14:53,120
consider it a loan.

352
00:14:53,480 --> 00:14:55,080
I'll definitely pay you back once I make money.

353
00:14:55,639 --> 00:14:58,480
These next few days are the most crucial.

354
00:14:58,799 --> 00:15:00,960
I can't go into battle without ammunition, can I?

355
00:15:01,879 --> 00:15:02,799
How much do you need?

356
00:15:05,200 --> 00:15:07,240
Let's get 15 tapes this time.

357
00:15:07,960 --> 00:15:09,600
Wait, didn't you just say ten?

358
00:15:09,639 --> 00:15:11,200
Why are there five more now?

359
00:15:11,279 --> 00:15:12,279
Are you eating these tapes?

360
00:15:12,679 --> 00:15:13,759
Mom.

361
00:15:14,200 --> 00:15:16,039
This subject is too rare.

362
00:15:16,360 --> 00:15:17,519
If I miss this chance,

363
00:15:17,519 --> 00:15:19,320
I might never get a second chance in my life.

364
00:15:19,679 --> 00:15:21,519
Once it's gone, it's gone!

365
00:15:21,960 --> 00:15:23,399
Come on, are you shaking me down?

366
00:15:24,080 --> 00:15:25,440
You expect me to sell everything I own?

367
00:15:25,840 --> 00:15:26,919
Mom, you're the best.

368
00:15:26,919 --> 00:15:28,600
I knew you'd help me out.

369
00:15:28,600 --> 00:15:29,159
Don't worry.

370
00:15:29,159 --> 00:15:30,679
As soon as I make money, I'll pay you right back!

371
00:15:47,360 --> 00:15:48,159
Reporter Shen.

372
00:15:48,240 --> 00:15:49,080
Here!

373
00:15:49,159 --> 00:15:49,720
Coming!

374
00:15:50,559 --> 00:15:51,519
Go ahead, sing, sing!

375
00:15:51,559 --> 00:15:52,039
Sing already!

376
00:15:52,720 --> 00:15:53,720
Sing! Come on, sing!

377
00:15:53,759 --> 00:15:54,320
Where's everyone?

378
00:15:56,240 --> 00:15:56,759
Where is everybody?

379
00:15:56,840 --> 00:15:57,200
Coming!

380
00:15:57,200 --> 00:15:58,120
Xiao Shen, didn't you say 6:30?

381
00:15:58,320 --> 00:15:59,080
You're the only one here.

382
00:15:59,159 --> 00:15:59,720
Sister Chunyan.

383
00:15:59,799 --> 00:16:00,759
Coming, coming!

384
00:16:00,759 --> 00:16:01,399
Aren't we right here?

385
00:16:01,399 --> 00:16:01,960
Old Cheng!

386
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:02,799
What are you dawdling for?

387
00:16:02,799 --> 00:16:03,559
You said 6:30.

388
00:16:03,840 --> 00:16:05,080
You office folks

389
00:16:05,120 --> 00:16:06,120
sure have it comfortable!

390
00:16:06,200 --> 00:16:06,840
Hurry up.

391
00:16:06,960 --> 00:16:07,639
Meeting time. Thanks, Sister Xuemei.

392
00:16:07,639 --> 00:16:08,200
Xuemei.

393
00:16:09,879 --> 00:16:10,279
Here.

394
00:16:10,279 --> 00:16:11,320
Reporter Shen, I'm here to serve you guys.

395
00:16:11,799 --> 00:16:12,240
Morning.

396
00:16:12,399 --> 00:16:13,320
Thanks.

397
00:16:13,600 --> 00:16:14,039
Here, take one.

398
00:16:14,200 --> 00:16:14,720
Quick.

399
00:16:14,879 --> 00:16:15,639
Where's Haipeng?

400
00:16:16,519 --> 00:16:17,679
Why isn't Zhao Haipeng here?

401
00:16:20,919 --> 00:16:21,720
Sister Xuemei is here.

402
00:16:27,159 --> 00:16:27,720
Hey, Haipeng.

403
00:16:30,639 --> 00:16:31,600
Look at you.

404
00:16:31,720 --> 00:16:32,320
Heading into battle,

405
00:16:32,320 --> 00:16:33,559
you can't go without ammo.

406
00:16:36,120 --> 00:16:36,639
Here.

407
00:16:40,759 --> 00:16:41,840
Where did you get this?

408
00:16:42,440 --> 00:16:43,600
I have connections in Lacheng.

409
00:16:44,360 --> 00:16:45,080
Had someone get it for me.

410
00:16:45,600 --> 00:16:46,559
What connections?

411
00:16:46,879 --> 00:16:48,000
You just bought it.

412
00:16:48,080 --> 00:16:48,840
What?

413
00:16:48,879 --> 00:16:49,480
What?

414
00:16:49,600 --> 00:16:50,480
Section Chief Zhao

415
00:16:50,679 --> 00:16:51,519
sold his TV,

416
00:16:51,960 --> 00:16:53,080
sold his motorcycle too.

417
00:16:53,879 --> 00:16:54,679
Spent all that money,

418
00:16:54,679 --> 00:16:56,200
and didn't even want anyone to know.

419
00:16:56,759 --> 00:16:58,519
I shouldn't have let you know.

420
00:16:58,919 --> 00:16:59,480
Come on, Director Cheng,

421
00:16:59,480 --> 00:17:00,960
why do you run your mouth so much?

422
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:03,639
Why don't you head to the broadcast room

423
00:17:03,639 --> 00:17:04,640
and give a speech?

424
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:07,119
College boy, don't listen to his nonsense.

425
00:17:07,839 --> 00:17:08,799
Write up a draft!

426
00:17:09,240 --> 00:17:10,720
Let's teach Section Chief Zhao

427
00:17:11,039 --> 00:17:12,200
how to pick up girls!

428
00:17:13,039 --> 00:17:14,039
Learn what from you?

429
00:17:14,039 --> 00:17:15,480
Learn how to stay a bachelor?

430
00:17:15,680 --> 00:17:16,000
Right!

431
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:17,519
You haven't even figured it out yourself!

432
00:17:18,039 --> 00:17:18,559
Come on, stop...

433
00:17:18,559 --> 00:17:19,079
Chuan, Chuan!

434
00:17:19,119 --> 00:17:20,359
You're a real pal!

435
00:17:20,920 --> 00:17:21,680
Off you go!

436
00:17:22,839 --> 00:17:23,440
Listen, listen...

437
00:17:23,440 --> 00:17:24,960
Leshui, don't listen to their racket.

438
00:17:25,839 --> 00:17:26,960
Here's how I see it.

439
00:17:27,680 --> 00:17:29,640
We recruited Leshui ourselves,

440
00:17:29,680 --> 00:17:30,440
right?

441
00:17:30,519 --> 00:17:32,240
Getting some tapes for the Publicity Section,

442
00:17:32,240 --> 00:17:33,440
isn't that totally normal?

443
00:17:33,519 --> 00:17:34,119
Spot on.

444
00:17:34,319 --> 00:17:34,960
Besides,

445
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:36,359
that TV was just sitting there.

446
00:17:36,440 --> 00:17:38,119
Nothing good was on lately anyway.

447
00:17:38,160 --> 00:17:39,319
It was just gathering dust there.

448
00:17:39,400 --> 00:17:39,839
Right?

449
00:17:40,079 --> 00:17:41,960
And that motorcycle was a real gas guzzler.

450
00:17:42,240 --> 00:17:42,799
Old Zhao...

451
00:17:44,039 --> 00:17:45,839
Wait, so you knew it guzzled gas?

452
00:17:46,079 --> 00:17:47,599
Then—then you forced it on me!

453
00:17:47,759 --> 00:17:48,119
Tieping...

454
00:17:48,119 --> 00:17:49,039
You even... you even threatened me!

455
00:17:49,039 --> 00:17:49,680
It's a great ride, though!

456
00:17:49,680 --> 00:17:50,680
Great ride? You even threatened me, saying

457
00:17:50,680 --> 00:17:51,000
if I didn't buy it,

458
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:52,119
- you'd cut ties! - I kept it so well!

459
00:17:52,160 --> 00:17:52,880
Give me a break!

460
00:17:52,880 --> 00:17:53,720
This cost hundreds!

461
00:17:53,720 --> 00:17:54,839
Such bull! He even borrowed money from you!

462
00:17:54,839 --> 00:17:55,759
- You shoot it. - It's over 200 a tape!

463
00:17:56,200 --> 00:17:57,240
Over 200 a tape!

464
00:17:57,240 --> 00:17:58,039
He must be up to his eyeballs in debt!

465
00:17:58,319 --> 00:17:59,400
- What did you think? - You really did it.

466
00:17:59,759 --> 00:18:00,319
All right, all right, all right.

467
00:18:00,359 --> 00:18:01,000
Keep it down.

468
00:18:01,039 --> 00:18:01,799
He's trying to work here.

469
00:18:03,960 --> 00:18:04,640
Is it turned on?

470
00:18:06,559 --> 00:18:07,359
Can you see clearly?

471
00:18:11,359 --> 00:18:12,240
I'm Shen Leshui,

472
00:18:13,119 --> 00:18:14,079
a Lacheng local,

473
00:18:15,240 --> 00:18:16,039
just a

474
00:18:16,240 --> 00:18:16,920
small-time director,

475
00:18:17,160 --> 00:18:17,839
a rookie reporter.

476
00:18:19,279 --> 00:18:20,319
No family background,

477
00:18:20,880 --> 00:18:21,599
and no money.

478
00:18:23,400 --> 00:18:24,759
We ran out of tapes.

479
00:18:25,680 --> 00:18:26,279
What now?

480
00:18:29,079 --> 00:18:30,519
Luckily, someone stepped up to help.

481
00:18:30,759 --> 00:18:31,880
Who?

482
00:18:31,920 --> 00:18:32,960
Me!

483
00:18:33,759 --> 00:18:35,599
Who else?

484
00:18:36,160 --> 00:18:37,160
Zhao Haipeng.

485
00:18:38,079 --> 00:18:38,359
Come on.

486
00:18:38,359 --> 00:18:38,920
She's calling you.

487
00:18:39,039 --> 00:18:39,680
Call... calling you.

488
00:18:39,759 --> 00:18:40,480
She's calling you! Wait, what do I do?

489
00:18:40,519 --> 00:18:41,160
Hurry up!

490
00:18:41,240 --> 00:18:41,759
Wait, wait, wait.

491
00:18:42,160 --> 00:18:42,680
No, no, no.

492
00:18:42,720 --> 00:18:43,480
No, no, no.

493
00:18:43,480 --> 00:18:44,119
Leave me out—wait,

494
00:18:44,119 --> 00:18:44,680
leave me out of this.

495
00:18:44,680 --> 00:18:45,119
Speak up properly.

496
00:18:45,119 --> 00:18:45,960
These tapes are expensive.

497
00:18:45,960 --> 00:18:47,160
Th-this is such a waste. It's recording!

498
00:18:47,160 --> 00:18:47,759
It's recording.

499
00:18:47,759 --> 00:18:48,519
Hurry up and talk!

500
00:18:48,680 --> 00:18:49,200
Alright, alright, alright.

501
00:18:49,200 --> 00:18:49,759
Come on, come on.

502
00:18:51,160 --> 00:18:51,680
Ms. Shen,

503
00:18:52,039 --> 00:18:52,599
ask away.

504
00:18:54,680 --> 00:18:55,960
All those new tapes,

505
00:18:56,200 --> 00:18:57,119
how did you get them?

506
00:18:58,279 --> 00:18:59,960
They must've cost quite a bit.

507
00:19:00,799 --> 00:19:02,119
Definitely didn't steal them.

508
00:19:02,119 --> 00:19:02,759
Well...

509
00:19:03,759 --> 00:19:04,920
here's how I see it.

510
00:19:05,039 --> 00:19:08,240
When money is spent on meaningful things,

511
00:19:08,240 --> 00:19:09,599
that's an honor for the money itself.

512
00:19:10,839 --> 00:19:11,680
Look at this kid.

513
00:19:12,839 --> 00:19:13,640
Smooth talker!

514
00:19:15,559 --> 00:19:16,799
Then why are you willing to help me?

515
00:19:18,359 --> 00:19:19,960
Didn't I just say? Why ask?

516
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:21,279
Because he likes you!

517
00:19:21,359 --> 00:19:23,119
Otherwise, why didn't he help me?

518
00:19:23,119 --> 00:19:24,440
What do you need tapes for anyway?

519
00:19:24,519 --> 00:19:25,759
Let me help, I'll tie a bow.

520
00:19:26,160 --> 00:19:26,839
Like this, like this, like this.

521
00:19:27,079 --> 00:19:27,799
Let's cut right to the chase,

522
00:19:27,880 --> 00:19:28,359
shall we?

523
00:19:28,480 --> 00:19:29,799
Just kiss her already!

524
00:19:29,920 --> 00:19:33,279
Kiss her! Kiss her!

525
00:19:33,359 --> 00:19:34,599
We're civilized folks. Kiss her!

526
00:19:34,680 --> 00:19:40,079
Kiss her! Kiss her! Kiss her!

527
00:20:07,920 --> 00:20:09,319
Now that the case is solved,

528
00:20:09,559 --> 00:20:11,799
Ms. Shen's in the mood to buy me dinner.

529
00:20:18,039 --> 00:20:18,720
What are we having?

530
00:20:19,279 --> 00:20:19,880
Hot pot.

531
00:20:21,599 --> 00:20:22,440
Hot pot, huh?

532
00:20:34,880 --> 00:20:37,160
Do you still remember our first meal?

533
00:20:39,240 --> 00:20:40,799
Xiaomei Hotpot.

534
00:20:42,079 --> 00:20:43,200
After that meal,

535
00:20:43,319 --> 00:20:45,359
our true revolutionary friendship began.

536
00:20:47,079 --> 00:20:48,079
And then?

537
00:20:48,559 --> 00:20:49,880
You went to Beijing to make your way,

538
00:20:50,759 --> 00:20:52,519
and I began my long wait.

539
00:20:54,519 --> 00:20:56,200
Only to end up with divorce papers.

540
00:20:57,200 --> 00:20:58,519
Hey, let's get the facts straight.

541
00:20:58,880 --> 00:21:00,880
You were the one who served me the papers.

542
00:21:01,519 --> 00:21:02,880
But you took them right away, didn't you?

543
00:21:04,960 --> 00:21:06,880
That's because I'm smart.

544
00:21:07,039 --> 00:21:07,839
Right?

545
00:21:08,279 --> 00:21:08,960
Here, give it to me.

546
00:21:10,559 --> 00:21:12,960
A wise man knows when to fold.

547
00:21:13,240 --> 00:21:13,880
You know?

548
00:21:14,279 --> 00:21:15,119
Making a scene and clinging on...

549
00:21:15,160 --> 00:21:16,000
I never do that.

550
00:21:18,400 --> 00:21:18,799
Cheers.

551
00:21:26,720 --> 00:21:27,960
The taste of Old Lapi Beer...

552
00:21:29,880 --> 00:21:31,559
I don't think it's as good as before.

553
00:21:32,160 --> 00:21:32,640
It's watered down.

554
00:21:38,920 --> 00:21:40,440
Signed the contract on this place yesterday.

555
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:44,680
Nice.

556
00:21:45,920 --> 00:21:46,559
So it's sold.

557
00:21:48,480 --> 00:21:49,839
Saves me from worrying whenever it storms,

558
00:21:49,839 --> 00:21:50,960
about the roof leaking.

559
00:21:54,079 --> 00:21:55,079
Once I get the money,

560
00:21:55,799 --> 00:21:56,799
I'll square things with you.

561
00:21:59,359 --> 00:22:00,880
There you go again.

562
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:04,079
Even close friends keep clean accounts.

563
00:22:06,599 --> 00:22:07,720
Honestly, Leshui,

564
00:22:09,119 --> 00:22:11,799
I was planning that when you remarry,

565
00:22:12,319 --> 00:22:13,480
I'd give you a huge gift.

566
00:22:14,519 --> 00:22:16,799
Back when the two of us tied the knot,

567
00:22:16,799 --> 00:22:18,200
we didn't even have a proper wedding.

568
00:22:19,160 --> 00:22:19,880
Stop right there.

569
00:22:21,559 --> 00:22:22,799
I'm doing just fine on my own.

570
00:22:23,880 --> 00:22:24,519
What's wrong?

571
00:22:24,920 --> 00:22:26,000
What rattled you?

572
00:22:27,319 --> 00:22:28,680
Who dumped you?

573
00:22:31,039 --> 00:22:32,279
I dumped myself.

574
00:22:35,000 --> 00:22:36,200
That's called making peace with yourself.

575
00:22:36,200 --> 00:22:36,880
You know that?

576
00:22:37,880 --> 00:22:39,480
Only those who've figured things out

577
00:22:39,799 --> 00:22:40,680
know how to make peace.

578
00:22:40,759 --> 00:22:41,960
People like me who haven't,

579
00:22:41,960 --> 00:22:43,359
you just stay stuck in endless turmoil,

580
00:22:43,880 --> 00:22:45,599
never grasping the truth of the universe.

581
00:22:47,039 --> 00:22:47,440
Come on.

582
00:22:48,440 --> 00:22:49,960
A toast to Ms. Shen, forty and doubt-free,

583
00:22:50,960 --> 00:22:53,079
seeing through everything under the sun.

584
00:22:56,119 --> 00:22:58,119
Seeing through everything?

585
00:22:58,440 --> 00:22:59,920
You'd have to live long enough to be a demon.

586
00:23:00,680 --> 00:23:02,720
I haven't even sorted out what's right before me.

587
00:23:03,240 --> 00:23:03,799
Really?

588
00:23:04,400 --> 00:23:05,119
Like what?

589
00:23:08,279 --> 00:23:09,119
Need to drink a bit more

590
00:23:09,319 --> 00:23:10,240
to have the guts to say it.

591
00:23:11,880 --> 00:23:12,480
Oh, man.

592
00:23:13,079 --> 00:23:13,680
Come on, let's go.

593
00:23:14,039 --> 00:23:14,720
I'll drink with you.

594
00:23:33,119 --> 00:23:33,920
Talk to me.

595
00:23:34,920 --> 00:23:36,000
What's weighing on your mind?

596
00:23:39,799 --> 00:23:41,119
Let me tell you,

597
00:23:41,400 --> 00:23:43,079
the past is in the past.

598
00:23:44,559 --> 00:23:45,039
Look,

599
00:23:45,599 --> 00:23:47,200
they caught everyone they were supposed to.

600
00:23:47,759 --> 00:23:48,319
Right?

601
00:23:50,240 --> 00:23:51,359
We've still got a long life ahead.

602
00:23:56,279 --> 00:23:56,640
Come on.

603
00:23:58,440 --> 00:23:59,160
At least...

604
00:24:00,200 --> 00:24:01,359
we're both still alive.

605
00:24:03,640 --> 00:24:04,400
Haipeng.

606
00:24:06,480 --> 00:24:07,720
Before we get drunk,

607
00:24:09,279 --> 00:24:10,599
I want to hear the truth.

608
00:24:13,880 --> 00:24:14,519
Go ahead.

609
00:24:20,160 --> 00:24:21,440
Do you remember

610
00:24:22,559 --> 00:24:24,319
that threatening letter I got back then?

611
00:24:25,839 --> 00:24:26,839
Of course I remember.

612
00:24:27,200 --> 00:24:28,839
It pissed me off so bad back then.

613
00:24:29,720 --> 00:24:31,640
That bastard still hasn't been found, right?

614
00:24:34,079 --> 00:24:35,599
Then do you remember

615
00:24:37,440 --> 00:24:39,519
what was written in that letter?

616
00:24:42,759 --> 00:24:45,319
"If you dare air the footage of the Lapi Brewery,

617
00:24:45,319 --> 00:24:46,240
you're dead."

618
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:48,559
Right?

619
00:24:50,000 --> 00:24:51,599
Can you believe that bastard...

620
00:24:58,480 --> 00:24:59,480
Back then, I only told you

621
00:24:59,480 --> 00:25:00,720
that I got a threatening letter.

622
00:25:01,839 --> 00:25:02,960
But I never told you

623
00:25:03,279 --> 00:25:04,519
what was in the letter.

624
00:25:07,759 --> 00:25:09,559
How do you know it so clearly,

625
00:25:12,200 --> 00:25:13,640
word for word?

626
00:25:41,240 --> 00:25:43,079
I always thought that threatening letter

627
00:25:43,079 --> 00:25:44,279
was written by Chen Qingchun.

628
00:25:47,559 --> 00:25:48,359
I never imagined

629
00:25:51,720 --> 00:25:53,319
it was actually you, Zhao Haipeng.

630
00:26:28,799 --> 00:26:29,680
Surprised, aren't you?

631
00:26:31,880 --> 00:26:32,960
I really did write it.

632
00:26:36,559 --> 00:26:37,359
Back then,

633
00:26:37,920 --> 00:26:38,880
I was just thinking...

634
00:26:38,960 --> 00:26:40,880
All that footage you shot,

635
00:26:41,960 --> 00:26:43,480
those scenes of people causing trouble,

636
00:26:45,279 --> 00:26:47,160
do you think Ma Guowen would let you air it?

637
00:26:47,799 --> 00:26:50,200
Would your station leaders agree to air it?

638
00:26:50,680 --> 00:26:51,480
Even...

639
00:26:51,880 --> 00:26:52,720
Cheng Youtian...

640
00:26:53,160 --> 00:26:54,519
None of them agreed.

641
00:26:56,799 --> 00:26:58,720
But look at the state you were in back then.

642
00:26:59,559 --> 00:27:01,039
You were completely hyped up,

643
00:27:01,039 --> 00:27:02,079
and I couldn't stop you.

644
00:27:05,200 --> 00:27:06,559
I had no choice but to resort to this.

645
00:27:11,880 --> 00:27:13,400
Then after Ma Guowen died,

646
00:27:14,519 --> 00:27:15,799
what about that threatening letter?

647
00:27:24,240 --> 00:27:24,759
Look,

648
00:27:25,720 --> 00:27:26,720
all I wanted was

649
00:27:27,119 --> 00:27:28,519
to get you out of here quickly.

650
00:27:31,759 --> 00:27:32,880
I tried to convince you so many times,

651
00:27:33,519 --> 00:27:34,240
but you wouldn't listen.

652
00:27:34,759 --> 00:27:36,039
The state you were in back then

653
00:27:37,279 --> 00:27:38,640
was just like all those years ago.

654
00:27:41,000 --> 00:27:42,960
So I had to pull the same trick again.

655
00:27:43,920 --> 00:27:46,359
You just didn't want me to see the discarded footage.

656
00:27:48,880 --> 00:27:49,480
What the hell are you talking about?

657
00:27:51,960 --> 00:27:53,440
Because in that footage,

658
00:27:54,319 --> 00:27:55,200
lies your secret.

659
00:27:58,960 --> 00:28:00,720
What secret could I possibly have?

660
00:28:05,720 --> 00:28:07,240
You took Liu Xuemei's money.

661
00:28:13,400 --> 00:28:14,839
I told you before

662
00:28:18,000 --> 00:28:20,279
that I filmed Liu Xuemei outside the auction house,

663
00:28:21,319 --> 00:28:22,920
running out clutching a bag,

664
00:28:23,440 --> 00:28:24,440
stumbling,

665
00:28:25,319 --> 00:28:26,279
as if she were drunk.

666
00:28:29,680 --> 00:28:31,759
Right after you watched that clip with me,

667
00:28:32,920 --> 00:28:34,359
I received that threatening letter.

668
00:28:39,200 --> 00:28:42,039
If I had edited those shots in,

669
00:28:43,119 --> 00:28:45,160
someone would have noticed.

670
00:28:47,359 --> 00:28:48,079
Because when the police

671
00:28:48,079 --> 00:28:50,039
arrived at the scene of Liu Xuemei's death,

672
00:28:50,079 --> 00:28:51,559
there was no bag to be seen.

673
00:28:52,920 --> 00:28:53,920
So nobody knew

674
00:28:53,920 --> 00:28:56,119
that there was once a bag filled with cash.

675
00:28:57,079 --> 00:28:59,359
That's the secret you hid for over a decade.

676
00:29:04,880 --> 00:29:06,839
You took that money.

677
00:29:30,519 --> 00:29:30,960
Hello?

678
00:29:31,079 --> 00:29:32,160
It's Zhao Haipeng from Publicity.

679
00:29:33,200 --> 00:29:33,920
Sister Xuemei,

680
00:29:35,480 --> 00:29:36,279
where are you?

681
00:30:04,240 --> 00:30:05,000
Zhao Haipeng!

682
00:30:07,799 --> 00:30:08,559
Zhao Haipeng!

683
00:30:11,039 --> 00:30:12,039
What are you doing here?

684
00:30:12,759 --> 00:30:13,559
Quick, quick, quick!

685
00:30:14,640 --> 00:30:15,200
Hurry!

686
00:30:15,200 --> 00:30:16,240
Come on, hurry, hurry!

687
00:30:17,880 --> 00:30:19,640
Wait, how much did you drink?

688
00:30:20,319 --> 00:30:22,079
You never drink!

689
00:30:22,319 --> 00:30:22,839
You... you...

690
00:30:23,240 --> 00:30:24,839
Who forced you to drink like this?

691
00:30:26,119 --> 00:30:26,559
By the way...

692
00:30:26,799 --> 00:30:27,279
Tell me...

693
00:30:27,839 --> 00:30:29,559
Why didn't you go to the auction?

694
00:30:29,720 --> 00:30:30,839
Someone sold us out.

695
00:30:31,119 --> 00:30:32,799
Ma Guowen knew all along that I was going.

696
00:30:33,200 --> 00:30:35,200
The second I arrived, I was cornered.

697
00:30:40,519 --> 00:30:41,359
Liu Xuemei.

698
00:30:41,960 --> 00:30:42,960
Director Ma is waiting for you.

699
00:30:44,759 --> 00:30:45,680
I have to get to the auction.

700
00:30:46,960 --> 00:30:48,240
Talk to Director Ma first.

701
00:30:48,799 --> 00:30:49,240
Move.

702
00:30:49,519 --> 00:30:50,559
I have to go to the auction! Let go!

703
00:30:50,920 --> 00:30:52,200
Talk after you see Director Ma.

704
00:30:52,200 --> 00:30:53,400
What are you doing?!

705
00:30:54,200 --> 00:30:54,799
Let go!

706
00:30:54,799 --> 00:30:55,319
Move!

707
00:30:56,599 --> 00:30:57,160
Then...

708
00:30:58,039 --> 00:31:00,200
he dragged me into a restaurant nearby.

709
00:31:00,359 --> 00:31:01,200
Someone was guarding the door.

710
00:31:01,440 --> 00:31:02,440
I couldn't get out at all.

711
00:31:03,920 --> 00:31:04,279
He...

712
00:31:04,759 --> 00:31:05,920
He pulled out 20,000 yuan,

713
00:31:06,079 --> 00:31:07,119
trying to shut me up.

714
00:31:14,599 --> 00:31:15,079
Wait here.

715
00:31:15,720 --> 00:31:16,920
The factory beauty lives around here, right?

716
00:31:17,440 --> 00:31:18,319
How should I know?

717
00:31:18,480 --> 00:31:20,240
What the hell are we looking for in this freezing cold?

718
00:31:20,440 --> 00:31:21,119
Just look when you're told to.

719
00:31:21,160 --> 00:31:22,119
Quit the damn whining.

720
00:31:22,160 --> 00:31:22,960
Quit arguing!

721
00:31:22,960 --> 00:31:23,920
You're distracting me from driving.

722
00:31:24,200 --> 00:31:25,359
Check up ahead. Look ahead.

723
00:31:25,359 --> 00:31:26,200
Over here!

724
00:31:26,440 --> 00:31:27,160
Slow down, slow down, slow down.

725
00:31:28,440 --> 00:31:29,559
Check up ahead. Look ahead.

726
00:31:30,079 --> 00:31:31,240
Where the hell is it?

727
00:31:35,079 --> 00:31:35,720
There's nothing here.

728
00:31:42,640 --> 00:31:45,039
I drank glass after glass to get this money.

729
00:31:45,480 --> 00:31:46,319
10,000 yuan a glass.

730
00:31:46,640 --> 00:31:48,759
I just wanted to get as much as I could.

731
00:31:48,960 --> 00:31:49,640
This... this...

732
00:31:49,640 --> 00:31:50,720
How much money is this?

733
00:31:52,160 --> 00:31:53,359
Exactly 200,000 yuan.

734
00:31:54,519 --> 00:31:55,119
I kept thinking...

735
00:31:55,480 --> 00:31:57,119
this is all our workers' money.

736
00:31:57,559 --> 00:31:58,599
We couldn't let him get away with it.

737
00:32:02,720 --> 00:32:04,000
Until the auction started,

738
00:32:04,160 --> 00:32:05,440
and I really couldn't drink anymore.

739
00:32:05,720 --> 00:32:06,880
That bastard Ma Guowen,

740
00:32:07,519 --> 00:32:08,440
he had evil intentions.

741
00:32:09,039 --> 00:32:10,119
He thought I was completely hammered.

742
00:32:10,480 --> 00:32:11,960
He planned to come back

743
00:32:12,640 --> 00:32:13,920
after the auction ended.

744
00:32:14,240 --> 00:32:15,319
He wanted to assault me.

745
00:32:15,799 --> 00:32:16,960
He thought I was dead drunk.

746
00:32:17,599 --> 00:32:18,480
Even though my legs gave out,

747
00:32:18,759 --> 00:32:19,839
my head was still clear.

748
00:32:20,559 --> 00:32:21,119
As soon as he left,

749
00:32:21,359 --> 00:32:22,240
I ran for it.

750
00:32:23,480 --> 00:32:24,880
I couldn't reach the finance office by phone.

751
00:32:25,359 --> 00:32:26,440
There were too many people in the workshop.

752
00:32:26,880 --> 00:32:28,039
You're the only one I could turn to.

753
00:32:30,079 --> 00:32:30,640
Take it.

754
00:32:30,920 --> 00:32:32,119
Why... why are you giving this to me?

755
00:32:33,079 --> 00:32:34,359
I haven't told a soul about this.

756
00:32:35,119 --> 00:32:36,319
Hurry up and take this money,

757
00:32:36,599 --> 00:32:37,720
and hide it somewhere safe.

758
00:32:38,799 --> 00:32:39,559
In all my life...

759
00:32:39,960 --> 00:32:40,279
I...

760
00:32:40,559 --> 00:32:41,960
I've never seen this much money.

761
00:32:42,880 --> 00:32:44,519
The thing is, where do I even hide it?

762
00:32:45,000 --> 00:32:46,039
Never mind where!

763
00:32:46,559 --> 00:32:47,920
The most important thing is to hide it!

764
00:32:48,200 --> 00:32:50,000
Ma Guowen knows where I live,

765
00:32:50,200 --> 00:32:51,000
right in this neighborhood.

766
00:32:51,319 --> 00:32:52,480
He won't let this go.

767
00:32:52,720 --> 00:32:53,599
You must hide it well.

768
00:32:54,039 --> 00:32:54,839
First thing tomorrow morning,

769
00:32:54,960 --> 00:32:56,119
we'll go find Director Cheng

770
00:32:56,319 --> 00:32:56,920
and see...

771
00:32:57,000 --> 00:32:58,000
how to distribute this money.

772
00:32:59,119 --> 00:33:01,119
I want to give this money back to those workers

773
00:33:01,799 --> 00:33:02,680
who chipped in to buy the factory,

774
00:33:03,000 --> 00:33:04,160
but feared retaliation

775
00:33:04,359 --> 00:33:05,880
and were afraid to claim their investment.

776
00:33:06,079 --> 00:33:06,880
Right, right, right.

777
00:33:07,480 --> 00:33:07,880
Right.

778
00:33:08,440 --> 00:33:09,000
Then... then...

779
00:33:09,759 --> 00:33:11,599
Then let me write you a receipt.

780
00:33:11,880 --> 00:33:12,759
Forget the receipt!

781
00:33:12,920 --> 00:33:13,880
There's no time for that!

782
00:33:14,000 --> 00:33:14,599
Just get out of here.

783
00:33:14,720 --> 00:33:15,640
Hurry and hide the money!

784
00:33:16,200 --> 00:33:16,720
Okay, okay.

785
00:33:17,200 --> 00:33:17,680
Go, hurry!

786
00:33:17,759 --> 00:33:18,160
Okay, okay.

787
00:33:18,160 --> 00:33:18,720
I trust you.

788
00:33:18,880 --> 00:33:19,480
Hurry up!

789
00:33:20,279 --> 00:33:21,400
See you at the publicity section tomorrow.

790
00:33:23,759 --> 00:33:24,240
Okay, okay.

791
00:33:24,359 --> 00:33:24,799
Go!

792
00:33:24,880 --> 00:33:25,640
See you tomorrow!

793
00:33:26,960 --> 00:33:28,279
Okay, okay, okay.

794
00:34:25,159 --> 00:34:26,039
Coming!

795
00:34:29,039 --> 00:34:29,679
Haipeng.

796
00:34:29,719 --> 00:34:30,239
Auntie.

797
00:34:30,440 --> 00:34:31,559
What brings you by?

798
00:34:32,239 --> 00:34:33,039
Where's Leshui?

799
00:34:33,360 --> 00:34:35,360
Isn't Leshui working late at the TV station?

800
00:34:35,400 --> 00:34:36,039
It's Millennium Eve,

801
00:34:36,119 --> 00:34:36,800
so I came to check on you.

802
00:34:37,159 --> 00:34:38,280
Working late again...

803
00:34:38,440 --> 00:34:39,280
You haven't eaten, have you?

804
00:34:39,480 --> 00:34:40,199
Not yet.

805
00:34:40,280 --> 00:34:41,159
Perfect timing. I'll make you something.

806
00:34:41,320 --> 00:34:41,960
Sounds great.

807
00:34:42,559 --> 00:34:43,159
Go sit over there.

808
00:34:43,679 --> 00:34:43,960
Okay.

809
00:34:43,960 --> 00:34:44,400
Give me a minute.

810
00:34:44,400 --> 00:34:45,079
Alright, okay.

811
00:34:45,800 --> 00:34:47,440
Anything warm will do, Auntie.

812
00:34:47,480 --> 00:34:48,079
Will do.

813
00:35:31,039 --> 00:35:31,760
Auntie.

814
00:35:32,719 --> 00:35:34,119
I heard they're setting off fireworks in People's Square.

815
00:35:34,119 --> 00:35:35,159
Aren't you going to watch?

816
00:35:36,199 --> 00:35:37,239
I'll pass.

817
00:35:37,239 --> 00:35:38,280
You young folks go have fun.

818
00:35:38,280 --> 00:35:39,119
Go with Leshui.

819
00:35:39,440 --> 00:35:40,320
All right, I'll go with Leshui then.

820
00:35:40,480 --> 00:35:41,320
Come back for dinner, okay?

821
00:35:41,639 --> 00:35:42,280
Come back and eat.

822
00:35:42,320 --> 00:35:42,719
Okay.

823
00:35:43,280 --> 00:35:44,280
I'm heading out now.

824
00:35:45,639 --> 00:35:46,400
Watch your step.

825
00:35:46,400 --> 00:35:47,159
Don't worry.

826
00:35:48,079 --> 00:35:49,079
Come back for dinner!

827
00:36:16,360 --> 00:36:16,920
Froze to death.

828
00:36:17,880 --> 00:36:18,840
It's a woman.

829
00:36:19,360 --> 00:36:20,039
Froze to death.

830
00:36:22,079 --> 00:36:23,320
Sir! Sir!

831
00:36:25,000 --> 00:36:25,679
What is it?

832
00:36:26,800 --> 00:36:28,079
Don't believe or spread rumors.

833
00:36:32,480 --> 00:36:33,039
Leshui.

834
00:36:40,599 --> 00:36:41,480
Liu Xuemei.

835
00:36:42,880 --> 00:36:43,400
What about her?

836
00:36:45,000 --> 00:36:47,519
The victim is Liu Xuemei.

837
00:36:57,119 --> 00:36:59,280
Director Ma is here with the security team.

838
00:37:00,079 --> 00:37:01,559
Do you want to head back to the factory first?

839
00:37:07,880 --> 00:37:08,400
Got it.

840
00:37:08,760 --> 00:37:09,639
I'm heading out.

841
00:37:27,320 --> 00:37:28,159
Something terrible happened.

842
00:37:28,360 --> 00:37:28,840
What's wrong?

843
00:37:29,400 --> 00:37:30,880
Liu Xuemei is dead.

844
00:37:31,159 --> 00:37:32,119
Don't cry yet.

845
00:37:32,679 --> 00:37:33,880
Because she's a traitor.

846
00:37:34,519 --> 00:37:36,280
She didn't even go to the auction.

847
00:37:36,280 --> 00:37:37,599
Ma Guowen gave her a huge sum of money.

848
00:37:37,639 --> 00:37:38,320
She took the cash and ran,

849
00:37:38,360 --> 00:37:39,440
and karma caught up with her.

850
00:37:39,679 --> 00:37:40,280
She's dead.

851
00:37:40,920 --> 00:37:41,719
But the problem is,

852
00:37:42,079 --> 00:37:43,000
she's dead,

853
00:37:43,360 --> 00:37:44,400
so where did the money go?

854
00:37:44,639 --> 00:37:45,360
Are you stupid?

855
00:37:45,840 --> 00:37:47,119
Someone killed her for the money!

856
00:37:50,639 --> 00:37:51,800
Who told you that?

857
00:37:52,000 --> 00:37:53,400
I heard it from Ma Guowen.

858
00:37:53,559 --> 00:37:54,840
It's all over the factory floor.

859
00:37:55,119 --> 00:37:56,239
You actually believe him?

860
00:37:56,280 --> 00:37:56,920
I don't believe his words,

861
00:37:56,920 --> 00:37:57,639
but I've got a brain.

862
00:37:57,880 --> 00:37:59,480
A woman with a child,

863
00:37:59,599 --> 00:38:00,960
with that much money in front of her...

864
00:38:01,000 --> 00:38:01,880
Who wouldn't be tempted?

865
00:38:02,079 --> 00:38:03,000
Could you resist?

866
00:38:07,079 --> 00:38:08,239
This is the meeting room.

867
00:38:08,360 --> 00:38:09,199
Ma Guowen is here.

868
00:38:09,199 --> 00:38:10,320
He brought the police with him.

869
00:38:14,199 --> 00:38:14,719
We're done for.

870
00:38:14,960 --> 00:38:15,840
They're questioning room by room.

871
00:38:16,039 --> 00:38:16,679
What do we do?

872
00:38:17,559 --> 00:38:18,599
What do you mean, "what do we do"?

873
00:38:19,239 --> 00:38:20,480
I didn't murder anyone for money.

874
00:38:20,480 --> 00:38:21,440
What do I have to be afraid of?

875
00:38:22,159 --> 00:38:23,480
Let them ask away.

876
00:38:25,719 --> 00:38:26,159
They're here! They're here!

877
00:38:26,199 --> 00:38:26,760
Hurry, let's go.

878
00:38:26,880 --> 00:38:27,880
This is the gatehouse.

879
00:38:28,039 --> 00:38:28,800
This is the security section.

880
00:38:29,079 --> 00:38:30,760
Behind these two is our section.

881
00:38:30,760 --> 00:38:31,400
The security section.

882
00:38:32,159 --> 00:38:32,679
Let's go.

883
00:38:35,079 --> 00:38:37,000
It's getting a bit late today.

884
00:38:39,239 --> 00:38:39,960
This is...

885
00:38:40,719 --> 00:38:42,119
the Women's Federation office.

886
00:38:42,800 --> 00:38:44,760
This is the deputy factory manager's office.

887
00:38:59,280 --> 00:39:00,920
It's getting pretty late today,

888
00:39:01,159 --> 00:39:01,679
but

889
00:39:01,960 --> 00:39:04,519
I'll round everyone up for you later, okay?

890
00:39:50,960 --> 00:39:53,039
I haven't told anyone about this.

891
00:39:53,440 --> 00:39:54,840
Make sure you find a safe place

892
00:39:55,039 --> 00:39:56,280
to hide this money.

893
00:40:09,960 --> 00:40:11,440
Ma Guowen won't just let this go.

894
00:40:11,599 --> 00:40:13,000
He'll definitely come back for me.

895
00:41:11,880 --> 00:41:12,800
Spendthrift.

896
00:41:32,719 --> 00:41:34,199
You really did hide the money

897
00:41:35,239 --> 00:41:37,039
in the safest place possible.

898
00:41:42,239 --> 00:41:43,719
No one would've ever guessed

899
00:41:44,760 --> 00:41:47,199
your true reason for never speaking ill

900
00:41:47,639 --> 00:41:48,800
of Liu Xuemei all these years.

901
00:41:51,920 --> 00:41:53,599
Because you were the only one who knew

902
00:41:54,880 --> 00:41:56,360
what kind of person she was.

903
00:41:59,800 --> 00:42:03,079
Yet you never once stepped forward to clear her name.

904
00:42:14,159 --> 00:42:15,400
Actually, I told them.

905
00:42:16,039 --> 00:42:17,960
I said Liu Xuemei wasn't that kind of person.

906
00:42:20,239 --> 00:42:21,559
But no one would listen to me.

907
00:42:22,880 --> 00:42:23,760
And no one believed me.

908
00:42:27,400 --> 00:42:29,519
If you had brought that money out

909
00:42:30,119 --> 00:42:31,599
and placed it before everyone,

910
00:42:32,000 --> 00:42:33,880
telling them what happened that night,

911
00:42:33,880 --> 00:42:35,719
would anyone still refuse to believe it?

912
00:42:38,280 --> 00:42:41,039
If Liu Tieping had known the truth,

913
00:42:42,199 --> 00:42:44,840
would he have done something so stupid?

914
00:42:46,239 --> 00:42:48,159
If Qian Yichuan had known the truth,

915
00:42:48,159 --> 00:42:50,159
would he have hurled such vile insults

916
00:42:50,280 --> 00:42:52,440
at such a kind-hearted woman?

917
00:42:55,039 --> 00:42:56,559
Every holiday,

918
00:42:57,679 --> 00:42:58,960
you threw money around,

919
00:42:59,079 --> 00:43:00,480
visiting the sick and the elderly.

920
00:43:03,400 --> 00:43:04,960
But did you ever tell them

921
00:43:04,960 --> 00:43:06,280
that this was the money Liu Xuemei

922
00:43:06,280 --> 00:43:08,039
fought so hard to get for them?

923
00:43:08,039 --> 00:43:10,280
That she drank glass after glass to get it?

924
00:43:13,199 --> 00:43:15,960
If she hadn't been forced to drink,

925
00:43:18,480 --> 00:43:20,079
she wouldn't have frozen to death.

926
00:43:21,719 --> 00:43:23,559
If she had known you'd turn out like this,

927
00:43:24,719 --> 00:43:26,719
she'd rather have gone to Cheng Youtian herself,

928
00:43:26,719 --> 00:43:28,199
and she wouldn't have frozen to death.

929
00:43:34,000 --> 00:43:34,800
Where's the money?

930
00:43:47,920 --> 00:43:48,440
Spent it.

931
00:43:58,760 --> 00:44:00,440
Have you ever searched your conscience?

932
00:44:01,960 --> 00:44:04,360
How do you face a soul that was misunderstood,

933
00:44:04,599 --> 00:44:05,840
slandered,

934
00:44:06,239 --> 00:44:08,480
and had its dignity trampled on?

935
00:44:09,320 --> 00:44:11,639
How do you face your own soul?

936
00:44:11,840 --> 00:44:13,440
Neither of us can withstand judgment.

937
00:44:14,719 --> 00:44:15,719
The judgment of the law.

938
00:44:16,559 --> 00:44:17,440
The judgment of morality.

939
00:44:18,039 --> 00:44:18,960
The judgment of conscience.

940
00:44:19,719 --> 00:44:21,880
Make more good films in the future.

941
00:44:22,239 --> 00:44:23,119
Films that are real,

942
00:44:23,920 --> 00:44:25,000
and deeply moving.

943
00:44:27,360 --> 00:44:27,960
Goodbye.
